# Long River Lurker: "When this creature enters, target creature you control can't be blocked this turn. Whenever that creature
# deals combat damage this turn, you may exile it. If you do, return it to the battlefield under its owner's control." On turn 3 the
# Lurker enters and makes Bot1's Grizzly Bears unblockable: Bot2's Ornithopter may not block it (CR 509.1b), the Bears deal 2 and
# Bot1 accepts: the Bears are exiled and come back untapped, a new object (CR 400.7), not attacking. Bot2's Ornithopter is
# refused as a target (a creature, but not Bot1's) (CR 115.1).

